  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Entrepreneurship ToT Panzi Foundation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The starting point of this project is the shared aim of the Panzi Foundation and Orange Corners to contribute to employment creation (SDG 8) and women socio-economic empowerment (SDG 10). The primary problem being addressed is the lack of entrepreneurial expertise among Panzi trainers, which hinders the effectiveness of the trainings given in the socio-economic pillar of the Panzi Foundation&#x2019;s programme. The project solves this problem through a comprehensive Training-of-Trainers (ToT) programme, which includes bassline assessments, curriculum development, and capacity-strengthening training modules. Panzi trainers will be equipped with the skills and tools necessary to provide high-quality entrepreneurial training to the Panzi participants. The goal is to strengthen the Panzi Foundation&#x2019;s capacity to deliver effective entrepreneurship training and create a pipeline for female entrepreneurs to participate in the Orange Corners programme, thus enhancing women&#x2019;s economic empowerment and supporting the overall entrepreneurial ecosystem in the Democratic Republic Congo.</narrative>
  </description>
